# agpkg manifest — required-tier software (docs/SYSTEM.md §6.1, M10).
# Format per line: <name> <url> <sha256> [core|opt] — 4th field optional,
# absent = core. core self-heals via `agpkg sync`; opt is user-picked
# (launcher "+" tile -> `agpkg opt-in`). ('#' comments, blank lines ok)
#
# M26: the default manifest is SIGNED — /etc/agpkg.manifest.sig holds a
# detached ed25519 sig over these raw bytes (same key/chain as agupd
# updates). sync/available/opt-in refuse an unsigned or tampered file;
# an explicit path argument stays unsigned (adb dev loop). Edit here =>
# re-sign on the host: agsign sign .local/keys/agupd.key <this file>
# (scripts/build-rootfs.sh does it automatically when the sig is stale).
#
# The sha256 pins content, so transport honesty is not load-bearing — but
# the canonical source is GitHub releases. On networks where GitHub stalls,
# prefix the URL with https://gh-proxy.com/ (sha256 still verified).
#
# An artifact may be a bare musl binary (v0 path) or a 四件套 tar
# (bin/<name> + pkg.toml + SKILL.md, required) — agpkg tells them apart
# by the ustar magic.
#
# aginx v0.3.2 and aginx-carrier v0.1.0 musl assets shipped 2026-08-30.
# The v0.2.1 carrier release was re-cut 2026-09-02 16:41Z with a new
# build (asset digest c0d490d3… per GitHub API) — the pin below follows
# the shipped asset, not the local build (bbac1017…) that preceded it.
# codex/grok have no usable upstream raw-musl asset (codex ships a tarball,
# grok has no musl release at all) — mirrored as raw binaries under
# yinnho/aginxos releases. aginxbrowser's UPSTREAM v0.2.5 musl asset
# segfaults on device (their CI zig was broken at tag time; fixed in
# b0315d7 after the tag) — same mirror treatment, device-verified rebuild
# (M10, /health + /fetch ok). All sha256 match the on-device installs.

aginx          https://github.com/yinnho/aginx/releases/download/v0.3.2/aginx-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl 1f8134d0d7bbead9ffcff9c7c1cb1499f3fcc10b4c7f3db7f44e41d658991690
aginx-carrier  https://github.com/yinnho/aginx-carrier/releases/download/v0.2.1/aginx-carrier-v0.2.1-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl c0d490d3f5f579f5e40c9e5972d89459997ed6357f9ee1fccea833ea40d97ba5
aginxbrowser   https://github.com/yinnho/aginxos/releases/download/aginxbrowser-v0.2.5/aginxbrowser-v0.2.5-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl 5561e6287d6b146a94170bb71fc2c5b0ff0e9e6cfd0aa0a8ea84a21d630a99e6
